      "writtenOn": "2023-09-05T11:37:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This test fails here.\nSTACKTRACE:\nhardware/interfaces/audio/aidl/vts/VtsHalAudioCoreModuleTargetTest.cpp:4037: Failure\nValue of: worker.hasError()\n  Actual: true\nExpected: false\nReceived ABORT from the logic cycle\nhardware/interfaces/audio/aidl/vts/VtsHalAudioCoreModuleTargetTest.cpp:4039: Failure\nValue of: driver.hasObservablePositionIncrease()\n  Actual: false\nExpected: true\n\ninRead recieves frames to be read as 0.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4188,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 4188,
        "endChar": 74
      },
      "revId": "a9e240b3e26d62d9cfc0a5b930eb9a595393ab68",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "54250419_8da299ba",
        "filename": "audio/aidl/vts/VtsHalAudioCoreModuleTargetTest.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 4188,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042638
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-05T23:29:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The error likely comes from the \"output\" part for the same reason I have explained in the `OutputDoesNotBlockWhenNoInput` test. Since `sendBurstCommands` joins the worker thread before returning, the writing part will never observe the reading, and thus its presentation counter will remain at zero.",
      "parentUuid": "95ea6a1e_676958e4",
